{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791567058,"nonce":"ligK195O41P6B/dGiT4YAhj92NY=","message":"Items 1 and 2 landed in 61bbe6b; item 3 is not done (see below).\n\n**Measured** (2026-10-09, Node 24.2.0, M-series Mac, release addon; node --expose-gc benchmarks/reactive-memory.mjs 100000; process footprint per item from footprint -p after GC with finalizer ticks; \"alive\" while 100,000 items exist, then after each of six make/dispose rounds; V8 heapUsed per item alive in brackets)\n\nBefore (e17be13):\n- closure in a JS array: alive 372 [201]; rounds 390, 422, 422, 430, 431, 433\n- signal: alive 798 [235]; rounds 583, 981, 1263, 1229, 1235, 1083\n- computed: alive 2064 [484]; rounds 1837, 2536, 2574, 2606, 2767, 2740\n- effect: alive 1711 [563]; rounds 1438, 1750, 2270, 2440, 2413, 2404\n\nAfter (61bbe6b):\n- closure in a JS array: alive 364 [201]; rounds 393, 422, 423, 424, 425, 425\n- signal: alive 309 [99]; rounds 373, 484, 488, 490, 495, 479\n- computed: alive 1178 [365]; rounds 1157, 1681, 1708, 1685, 1697, 1713\n- effect: alive 1012 [445]; rounds 1168, 1687, 1886, 2042, 2028, 2116\n\nSo alive: signal -61%, computed -43%, effect -41%. Not yet the 0.5 KB the plan expected for computeds and effects.\n\n**What changed**\n- NativeGraph takes keys: signal()/computed(id)/effect(id) return a number (slot index in the low 32 bits, a 21-bit generation above); track/peek/notify/trackComputed/release take keys. Stale, foreign-kind and malformed keys are rejected as disposed. No napi class per item.\n- One FunctionRef per context (the dispatcher passed to the constructor); the graph's per-item closure captures only the dispatcher's address and the callback id. ReactiveContext keeps callbacks in an array with a free list.\n\n**Item 3 (due effects returned as ids, run by JS) is not possible on blinc_core today.** An effect's dependencies are tracked while it runs inside ReactiveGraph::run_effect, which is private; an effect run by JavaScript after the flush would track nothing. The dispatcher is still called once per due effect from inside the flush. Doing it needs blinc_core to expose either run_effect or a tracking scope (begin/end observer) so JS can run an effect between two native calls, which would be two calls per effect, not fewer. Left as is.\n\n**Where the rest goes, for a next step**\n- JS per effect beyond the user's closure: the registered closure, the returned Disposable and its dispose closure, the Scope made for each run, and the #owned Set entry (heap 445 vs 201 for the bare closure). Creating the Scope lazily and folding the Disposable into one class would trim it.\n- Native per effect: blinc_core's effect node, blinc_abi's EffectKey (two Rc cells, two allocations), the boxed graph closure wrapping ours, and our slot.\n- After disposal, effect rounds still creep for a few rounds before levelling, as they did before; the closure control levels at about 420.","files":null}]}